  "body": "Stacked on #2731. Merge #2731 first (retarget order: AGENTS.md \"Overlapping issues stack\"). Until then, the diff against `main` also shows the #2731 commits.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `step_fit.rs`: `fit()` returns `Result<Fit, &'static str>`. Each silent `return KEPT` of the parameter check is now an `Err` with a reason:\n  - no surface parameters;\n  - parameters that do not give the mesh's points;\n  - a facet that is not a triangle;\n  - a point index that the mesh does not hold;\n  - more points than the fit can count;\n  - a pass tolerance that is not positive;\n  - no surface in the shell (in `fit_face`).\n- A new `judged(index, fit)` takes the result for face `index`. On `Err` it logs `step: face <n> keeps the kernel's facets unmeasured (<reason>); the model is reduced fidelity` and reports the face as `UNMEASURED` (1000 file units). The model is then reduced fidelity (#864) and verify refuses.\n- `fit_face` takes the face index. `step.rs` passes it on the same line (the file stays at 400 lines).\n- Decision entry: `docs/decisions/2719-step-fit-fallback-diagnostic.md` (mark, not measure; why).\n\n## Readings\n\n- Fallback, no parameters (face index 3): log `step: face 4 keeps the kernel's facets unmeasured (its mesh carries no surface parameters); the model is reduced fidelity`. Reported height: before 0 (full fidelity, no log); after 1000 file units.\n- Fallback, parameters 0.1 mm off the points (face index 0): log `step: face 1 keeps the kernel's facets unmeasured (its mesh's parameters do not give its points); the model is reduced fidelity`. Reported height: before 0; after 1000 file units.\n- Bar fixture `bar_cross_holes.step`: 0.005 mm before and after (no fallback on it). No STEP fixture in the 22 quick-gate suites goes to reduced fidelity.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/app/src/geometry/import/step_fit_tests.rs` (lib):\n- `a_face_without_surface_parameters_is_logged_and_reported_unmeasured`\n- `a_face_whose_parameters_miss_its_points_is_logged_and_reported_unmeasured`\n\nEach captures the log, and asserts the face number and the reason in it. It asserts that the kernel's facets are kept and that the face reports `UNMEASURED`, also through `step_facets::facets_of`. It asserts that `step::coarse` gives reduced fidelity for each file unit from the micrometre to the kilometre, and that the value is never the unknown-fidelity sentinel.\n\nQuick gate on head 1111b8402: 22 steps, 0 failed. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real STEP file from a different writer that causes the fallback. The pins use synthetic meshes.\n- The refusal that the user sees is the general `TOO_COARSE` text (\"re-import with a larger STEP facet budget\"). A larger budget does not help an unmeasured face. Only the log names the true cause. Follow-up filed (see the issue comment).\n- The kept mesh of an unmeasured face is not measured (the decision entry says why).\n- `feature_edge_g1_join` (#2713) is not in the quick plan of this diff.\n\nChangelog: STEP import logs a curved face whose facets it cannot measure, and marks the model reduced fidelity so that verify refuses, in place of a silent full-fidelity import.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2719\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
